<title>GERMANY: East German Apr industry output rises 2.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>East German Apr industry output rises 2.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following indicator:</p>
<p>E.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Apr 97     Mar 97	Apr 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)  +2.2	 +2.8	 +12.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.7	+11.7	  +6.8</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     146.7	143.6	 144.2</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Apr 97		  Mar 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   167.7	+0.7     166.6	 +4.4</p>
<p>Including:</p>
<p>  Intermediate goods    198.5	+1.0     196.6	 +3.9</p>
<p>  Capital goods	   140.1	-3.6     145.4	+10.7</p>
<p> Energy output	     90.0	+7.5	83.7	 +1.5</p>
<p> Construction	     194.1	+2.2     190.0	 -0.4</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-Mar 97 with Feb-Jan 97:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +9.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-Mar 97 with Apr-Mar 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +6.2</p>
<p> Mining				     -11.7</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		   +9.6</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	+13.3</p>
<p>		Capital goods	     +10.4</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	  +5.6</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	     +1.5</p>
<p> Energy output			     -4.1</p>
<p> Construction				+5.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-28-26097150</p>
</text>
